{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"c03fe4ebf3b5bae54d6b6f3bace85c2d155fde3641d9213acee73c06a365feee","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_372a6c227c50e9c9228ab62ea2f58a0a0a2f3ad87e4bf3856c8d6f7e676ce97f","overall_assessment":"The paper is well-organized with a logical flow from background to method and experiments. The writing is generally clear, though minor typographical errors and inconsistent capitalization of the acronym 'FiGAR' slightly detract from the polish. Mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined, and the provided tables are readable and informative.","paper_id":"B1GOWV5eg","paper_identity_sha256":"fc4d58c677ff11cd5f379613c95492568f577e64622c15bc80f3dfe89a10e5f7","prompt_identity_sha256":"7fbaec9cf2ace5038c34741c09df8b3ed34aa0f4c3b52cae509a2db542f20a01","raw_response_sha256":"51fdd651d604d983da0538a25ec616af6f5b4358b085913d966ed84a297e0a65","request_identity_sha256":"a61b6e0f111fe10936c68ea7ace7c2c76175fd64bbdfa4e1428fa730355eadc5","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"fd4aa263064d1ab5f889e80009f6aa549ec81efc4210768658e83355c6b2a9ed","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, moving logically from the introduction of the problem to the background, the proposed FiGAR framework, and finally the experimental results. The writing is generally clear and concise. However, there are minor typographical issues that affect the professional presentation. For instance, in Section 4, the text reads 'In tradition DRL algorithms' instead of 'In traditional DRL algorithms'. Additionally, the acronym for the proposed method is inconsistently capitalized as 'FiGAR' in most of the text but appears as 'FIGAR-DDPG' in Section 5.3. Correcting these minor errors would improve the overall clarity and polish of the manuscript.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-022"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined throughout the paper. The authors clearly define the policy components (pi_theta_a and pi_theta_x) and the action repetition set R. The derivations for the modified objective functions in the FiGAR-A3C and FiGAR-TRPO sections are presented clearly, with the specific combination operators (addition and multiplication) explicitly stated. The notation for the advantage function and the KL-divergence constraint is standard and easy to follow.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-027","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The Markdown tables provided in the text are readable and well-structured. Table 1 clearly presents the action repetition distribution across different games, and Table 2 provides a clear comparison of the performance of FiGAR-TRPO and TRPO on MuJoCo tasks. The captions for the figures and tables are descriptive and provide sufficient context for the reader to understand the data presented. The textual descriptions of the figures, such as the explanation of the arrows and thunderbolts in Figure 1, are detailed and helpful for interpreting the visual content.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"ce255b80b0d65a6f922b87150eb78835e594bd52cdfd648a5de1520f818ec7d0","paper_id":"B1GOWV5eg","paper_ordinal":6,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"51fdd651d604d983da0538a25ec616af6f5b4358b085913d966ed84a297e0a65","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1GOWV5eg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"8659b9a49cba08d0406b691e4016ac0002e5068aef564857d660adf7c4f86e5a","request_identity_sha256":"a61b6e0f111fe10936c68ea7ace7c2c76175fd64bbdfa4e1428fa730355eadc5","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":612,"prompt_tokens":1